-4c20-9b77-2e2fb4b9dc53","oracle_text":"As this creature enters, choose a player.\nIf a source would deal damage to the chosen player or a permanent they control, it deals double that damage instead.","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2024-06-14","toughness":"4","type_line":"Creature — Dinosaur"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":["R"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{R}","name":"Shock","oracle_id":"a9d288b8-cdc1-4e55-a0c9-d6edfc95e65d","oracle_text":"Shock deals 2 damage to any target.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it.","oracle_id":"049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If another effect (or effects) modifies how much damage a source would deal to the chosen player or a permanent they control (for example, by preventing some of that damage), the player being dealt damage or the controller of the permanent being dealt damage chooses the order in which any such effects, including the effect of Sawhorn Nemesis, apply. If all of the damage is prevented before Sawhorn Nemesis's effect would apply, its effect no longer applies.","oracle_id":"2f9107c5-991a-4c20-9b77-2e2fb4b9dc53","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If damage dealt is being divided or assigned among multiple permanents or players, that damage is divided or assigned before any effects that modify how much damage will be dealt. For example, if you attack the chosen player with a 5/5 creature with trample and it's blocked by a 2/2 creature they control, you can assign 2 damage to the blocker and 3 damage to the defending player. Those amounts are then doubled to 4 and 6, respectively.","oracle_id":"2f9107c5-991a-4c20-9b77-2e2fb4b9dc53","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The damage is dealt by the same source as the original source of damage. The doubled damage isn't dealt by Sawhorn Nemesis unless it was the original source of damage.","oracle_id":"2f9107c5-991a-4c20-9b77-2e2fb4b9dc53","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The protector of a battle with the Siege subtype is not that battle's controller.","oracle_id":"2f9107c5-991a-4c20-9b77-2e2fb4b9dc53","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This card now uses the Reach keyword ability to enable the blocking of flying creatures. This works because a creature with flying can only be blocked by creatures with flying or reach.","oracle_id":"e740ce2f-2134-473c-afa1-1b6d2d1e38ef","published_at":"2008-04-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
